# STEMROBIN-182/current182-4 Independent Figure Review

Result: **REVISE**. Scope is only draft fig-62, fig-63, fig-64. Preview recovery
passed; source fidelity and label clearance did not pass for both graphs.
No author/spec/SVG edits, promotion, finalization, or durable review occurred.

## Findings

1. **fig-63: missing source dashed domain-endpoint guide.** The native source has a
   deliberately dashed vertical line at mathematical `x=6`, between `(6,3)` and
   `(6,0)`. It is visible near native `x=464..471`, `y=80..260`; the indispensable
   crop is source rectangle `[427,64,486,271]`. Consecutive native dark runs at
   that column include `y=90..110`, `116..139`, `146..173`, `180..204`,
   `209..233`, and `238..249`, unlike adjacent near-continuous grid columns.
   This patterned boundary guide is not random scan damage. The current preview
   has only a continuous grid stroke there: at 640 width, approximately
   `x=473.04`, `y=111.30..278.26`. All visible SVG strokes compute `dasharray:
   none`. The source inventory's blanket scan-artifact classification omits
   this source requirement, and no mapped object/assertion preserves it.

2. **fig-63: origin label intersects the y-axis.** `source-x-value-0` is anchored
   at `(0,-0.48)`, centered on the continuous axis `x=0`. Browser text rectangle
   at 640 width is `[133.81,292.43,10.64,21.50]`; the axis is `x=139.13` over
   `y=66.78..389.57`, crossing through the label. The already observed neutral
   preview confirms the stroke through `0`. The original separates the printed
   `0` from its y-axis. A passed renderer label report does not settle this
   actual browser overlap.

3. **fig-64: missing source dashed domain-endpoint guide.** The native source has
   a deliberately dashed vertical guide at mathematical `x=-2`, between
   `(-2,3)` and `(-2,0)`. It appears near native `x=42..51`, `y=79..255`; crop
   rectangle `[29,62,76,267]`. Native dark runs include `y=90..123`,
   `129..154`, `164..189`, `205..229`, and `235..249`, with repeated multi-pixel
   gaps rather than incidental one-pixel scan breaks. The current continuous
   grid stroke at 640 width is approximately `x=83.48`,
   `y=111.30..278.26`. No visible dashed object or source-inventory assertion
   covers the guide.

4. **fig-64: origin label intersects the y-axis.** `source-x-value-0` is anchored
   at `(0,0.45)`, centered on `x=0`. Its actual 640-width text rectangle is
   `[189.46,240.68,10.64,21.50]`; the axis is `x=194.78` over
   `y=66.78..389.57`, passing through the label. The source printed origin label
   is separated from the axis. The neutral preview was observed once and
   confirms this overlap.

Authorized author follow-up should retain these source dashed guides and give
both origin labels clear space without changing coordinates, curve values,
domains, grid counts, or adding query/solution annotations. This reviewer did
not perform that follow-up.

## Checks

- **fig-62: independent bounded figure checks PASS.** One shared two-circle
  frame, two crossings, neither set contained in the other, horizontal Z
  hatching and vertical P hatching both continue into the shared lens. Source
  pixel cross-sections distinguish 13 interior horizontal rows and 14 vertical
  stripes; the modern figure retains 13/14 logical stripes, split into 15/16
  segments only for the two name clearances. Z and P remain inside their own
  non-overlap lobes. No points, members, region answers, frame, or captions were
  added. Circle rectification, equal radius, exact stripe spacing, and clean
  typography are disclosed modern regularizations, not asserted source units.
- Both source graph grids were independently observed as 19 vertical / 13
  horizontal lines, hence **18 columns x 12 rows**, with **0.5-unit cells on
  both axes**. Source bounds remain fig-63 `[-1.5,7.5] x [-2,4]` and fig-64
  `[-2.5,6.5] x [-2,4]`. One coordinate frame, positive arrow directions,
  integer tick labels, a single printed zero, and no physical units are kept.
  There are no added printed half-unit tick values.
- Curve shape, connected spans, solid stroke, and endpoint domains are retained:
  fig-63 `[-1,6]`, endpoints `(-1,-1)` and `(6,3)`; fig-64 `[-2,5]`, endpoints
  `(-2,3)` and `(5,-1)`. No endpoint dots, new curve names, filled regions,
  query lines, formulas, or solutions appear. Independent native-grid
  registration at 14 non-grid-column locations per curve yields maximum
  vertical discrepancies below 0.08 unit for fig-63 and 0.053 for fig-64.
  This approximate scan/thickness check is not recovery of an exact function.
- Full relevant modern text for **913/938/939**, including all a/b/c tasks and
  the shared final example request in 913, was compared to each figure context.
  It matches the current template SHA-256
  `5991dd79d140b2a3d8f746edea2dcbfabed19d86f593aaad72d3ec8a0e931fa6`.
  Existing FIRST text-review PASS for 153 items is reused, not repeated; it
