## Preview Recovery

The installed app Playwright 1.61.1 launched **headed Chromium** successfully,
rendering exact current SVG bytes via offline `setContent` HTML. Only wrapper
width and inherited semantic CSS roles were applied. No SVG colors, geometry,
attributes, author files, or specs were replaced. CSS mappings are extracted
from the actual local `app/src/styles/app.css`, with their hash retained.
There were no page errors or requested external page resources; the browser
closed at completion.

At actual **640 x 480** browser media size:

| Figure | Min Text | Non-Text Pixels | Dark Non-Text Pixels | Visible Semantic Geometries |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| fig-62 | 27.826 px | 25,019 | 17,555 | 33 |
| fig-63 | 19.130 px | 24,073 | 3,721 | 54 |
| fig-64 | 19.130 px | 24,249 | 3,858 | 52 |

All neutral/accent/print screenshots numerically pass nonblank, not-text-only,
and per-geometry pixel-presence checks. Minimum geometry-probe hit fractions
are at least 0.966. These are actual screenshots, not DOM-only or inventory
counts. Text is also at least 16 px at the declared 736-width canvas.
The local HTML's 390-width scroll container reaches `scrollLeft=250` for its
640-width media. This is a local wrapper check, not a new product measurement.

The successful unchanged-SVG browser strokes settle the earlier missing-stroke
preview as a **legacy raster-tool limitation** consistent with its CSS-variable
diagnosis. No legacy raster rerun or old failed-preview image observation was
needed. Successful technical recovery does not approve either graph.

